Now I have the full picture. Let me compile the formal audit.

---

## testsmells.org 19-Smell Academic Audit

**Scope:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` — 8 test methods, MSTest 4.1, .NET 10
**Integration calibration:** Class is `[TestCategory("Integration")]` — Mystery Guest / Eager Test severity downgraded per calibration rules. Sleepy Test remains High per research consensus (Spadini et al., MSR 2020).

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 93)
**Problem:** `if`/`else` branches execute different assertions — one branch may **never** run, hiding a gap.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — branching assertions
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests, one per type:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<PremiumUser>(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** If `GetByEmail` never returns `PremiumUser`, the discount assertion silently never executes — a hidden testing gap.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell #3)

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)
**Problem:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` introduces a hard 3-second wall-clock wait. This is non-deterministic (may be too short on slow CI, always too long locally) and inflates suite runtime.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — hard sleep
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout or use an async event signal:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll up to 5 s, checking every 100 ms
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
    {
        Assert.IsTrue(DateTime.UtcNow < deadline, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
}
```

**Additional note:** The method is `async Task` but uses synchronous `Thread.Sleep` instead of `await Task.Delay` — this blocks the thread pool thread unnecessarily.

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures on slow machines; guaranteed 3 s of wasted time on every run even when the event fires in 50 ms. Research (Camara et al., SAST 2021) correlates Sleepy Test with flaky test rates.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)
**Problem:** Executes 100 inserts but **asserts nothing**. MSTest reports this as "passed" even if every insert silently corrupts data.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertions
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Fix:** Assert on the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — code coverage looks great (100 insert calls exercised) but zero behavior is verified.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Smell)

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)
**Problem:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails, the MSTest output says only `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>.` without indicating *which property* failed.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — 4 bare assertions
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add assertion messages:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned as a positive integer.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower failure diagnosis, especially in CI logs where you can't set breakpoints.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining 4 tests are **well-designed** for their integration context:

| Test | Why it's clean |
|------|----------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior verified with `Assert.IsNull` |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count `3` is contextually obvious (3 items just inserted) — not Magic Number |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimate multi-threaded integration test; count `10` matches `Range(0, 10)` |

The use of in-memory SQLite (`Data Source=:memory:`) is a **hermetic test fixture**, not a Mystery Guest — external resource coupling is absent. The `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` pair correctly scopes the connection per test (no General Fixture smell since both fields are used by all 8 tests).

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` | Eliminates false-pass risk; ~1 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** | Split `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` into 2 tests | Eliminates hidden gap; ~5 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** | Replace `Thread.Sleep(3000)` with polling loop | Eliminates flakiness + saves ~3 s/run; ~5 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** | Add message strings to `InsertUser` assertions | Improves diagnostics; ~2 min |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests have cataloged smells. The three High-severity findings (Assertion-Free, Conditional Logic, Sleepy) represent real correctness and reliability risks. The remaining 4 tests are solid. Fixing all four issues is roughly 15 minutes of work.
